Origin of the source files
--------------------------

Ported from Symphonia (symphonia-codec-aac 0.5.5 and symphonia-core 0.5.5,
https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia), Copyright (c) 2019-2023 The Project
Symphonia Developers, which includes code originally written for NihAV by
Kostya Shishkov and relicensed for Symphonia with his permission. These files
keep their original MPL-2.0 headers and were modified for LingOS (no_std +
alloc, libm maths, crate-local bit reader and Huffman decoder, extra input
validation, bug fixes noted in the file headers):

  src/lib.rs        (AudioSpecificConfig parsing and the element loop)
  src/common.rs
  src/cpe.rs
  src/dsp.rs
  src/ics.rs        (ics/{mod,pulse,tns,ltp,gain}.rs merged)
  src/imdct.rs      (IMDCT from symphonia-core dsp/mdct)
  src/tables.rs     (AAC Huffman code tables)
  src/window.rs

Written for LingOS (also MPL-2.0, as part of this crate):

  src/bits.rs, src/huffman.rs, the FFT in src/imdct.rs,
  src/sbr/mod.rs    (spectral band replication, from ISO/IEC 14496-3 4.6.18)
  src/sbr/tables.rs (constant tables of ISO/IEC 14496-3: QMF window, noise
                     table, SBR Huffman tables; generated by
                     tools/gen-sbr-tables.py)
  tests/, tools/

Test vectors are generated locally by tools/gen-testdata.sh (FFmpeg and
libfdk-aac on the host); they are not part of the crate.
